# Terraform working directories and run output.
#
# This repository had no ignore file until hosted#159. A `terraform init` in
# any root writes a provider cache of several hundred megabytes, and one
# `git add <dir>` then tries to push it. GitHub refuses the push, which is the
# good case; the bad case is a repository nobody can clone.
#
# The provider lock file is NOT ignored. No root commits one today, so it stays
# visible in `git status` rather than hidden by a rule.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan

# The terraform exit test writes both of these into the root it plans, and
# uploads them as run artifacts.
plan.json
plan.log

# Python bytecode that a guard or a probe writes when it imports a sibling
# module. hosted#513 committed two files by accident.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The S3 backend of stage 0 for an env that keeps it in AWS (drill).
# scripts/stage0-store.sh writes it before each init and removes it for an env
# that keeps stage 0 on the workstation.
substrate/gibson-bootstrap/backend_override.tf
